What:           /dev/s31-overlay
Date:           September 2026
Contact:        ESP32-S31 port maintainers
Description:
                Private runtime device-tree overlay misc device (not configfs).
                The UAPI is include/uapi/linux/esp32s31-overlay.h.
                write() submits one complete DTBO of at most 128 KiB. The
                manager checks names, GPIO claims and exclusive resources.
                At most 32 overlays are active simultaneously.

                S31_OVERLAY_IOC_GET_LAST_ID returns the last applied integer ID.
                S31_OVERLAY_IOC_LIST returns count and active items; each item
                has a signed ID, 32-byte name and aligned 64-bit GPIO mask.
                S31_OVERLAY_IOC_REMOVE_NAME removes the named overlay.
                S31_OVERLAY_IOC_REMOVE_ALL removes active overlays in reverse
                application order. A failure can leave later entries removed.
                ioctl values and structure padding are part of the ABI; use
                the shared header rather than a private copy.

                Permissions on the device node control access. Invalid blobs,
                names, sizes, unavailable resources and busy removals return
                negative errno. Successful application does not prove external
                hardware behavior. The kernel does not save boot policy;
                s31-overlay manages that policy and its userspace lock.
